-- A row of ten oil cells produced from the last one, with a numerical aquifer
-- of three cells attached to the first.  The aquifer cells lie below the
-- water-oil contact, deepening away from the reservoir, and take their initial
-- pressure from equilibration, so nothing flows until the producer draws the
-- pressure down.  Water then moves along the row and reaches the producer.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
COMPOSITIONAL NUMERICAL AQUIFER WITH A PRODUCER

METRIC

OIL
GAS
WATER

DIMENS
13 1 1 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP

TABDIMS
/

EQLDIMS
/

WELLDIMS
1 1 1 1 /

AQUDIMS
3 1 /

START
1 'JAN' 2020 /

UNIFOUT

GRID

INIT

DX
13*25 /
DY
13*50 /
DZ
13*10 /
TOPS
13*2000 /

PORO
13*0.25 /
PERMX
13*200 /
PERMY
13*200 /
PERMZ
13*200 /

-- Cells 11-13 become the aquifer.  The initial pressure is defaulted.
AQUNUM
-- ID  I  J K  AREA    LENGTH  PORO  PERM  DEPTH  PRESSURE
   1   11 1 1  2.0E4   3000    0.25  50    2030   1* /
   1   12 1 1  2.0E4   3000    0.25  50    2060   1* /
   1   13 1 1  2.0E4   3000    0.25  50    2090   1* /
/

AQUCON
-- ID  I1 I2 J1 J2 K1 K2  FACE
   1   1  1  1  1  1  1   'I-' /
/

